# Local context (not versioned)

Copy this file to `CLAUDE.local.md` and fill it in. Git ignores `CLAUDE.local.md`, so it never leaves this machine.

## What goes here

- Local paths: where the repository, tools and data live on this machine.
- Private pointers: where the notes, tickets or documents that are not part of the repository can be found.
- Machine notes: installed versions, services that must be running, shell quirks.
- Personal preferences for how to work with the assistant, such as tone or language of the conversation.

## What does not go here

- Secrets, tokens and passwords. Use environment variables or a secret manager.
- Anything the project needs to work for other people. That belongs in versioned files such as `CLAUDE.md` or `docs/`.

## Rule for agents

No agent file, brief or versioned document may refer to `CLAUDE.local.md`. Its content is only for the main session on this machine, and what it says must never be copied into anything that is committed.

## Example

```text
Repository: ~/projects/my-project
Notes: the project wiki, page "Status"
Machine: Node 24 via a version manager; run `nvm use` first
```
